/E (3\) RL is very good and also very messy. Now you can see why I started with FWG RPS-- they're diagnostics to see whether my RL code was working in the domain. I would say that it depends a lot on the scope that you set. If you re-examine the little cup project you can also kind of see why I used a genetic algorithm-- it was a signal from noise machine anyway, but I had a hardcoded evaluation function \(my beliefs\) and no idea how to find the team. That is a very nice setting for a GA IMO. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [38]
